   "title": "Nine variants on one 9x9",
   "rules_text": "Sudoku: Place 1–9 in every row, column and 3×3 box.\nKiller: Digits in a cage sum to its small clue and don't repeat within the cage.\nArrow: Digits along an arrow sum to the number in its circle.\nThermo: Digits strictly increase along a thermometer from the bulb.\nGerman Whispers: Adjacent digits on a whisper line differ by at least 5.\nRenban: A renban line holds a set of consecutive digits in any order, without repeats.\nBetween Lines: Digits on a between line lie strictly between the digits in its end circles.\nKropki: Digits separated by a white dot are consecutive; digits separated by a black dot are in a 1:2 ratio.\nXV: Digits separated by a V sum to 5.\nOdd-Even: A digit in a grey square is even.",
